    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.basics\n\n### Description\n\nOS : Linux (Fedora 41)\r\nfzf : 0.57.0\r\n\r\nHello.\r\nThere is an issue where the letter \"i\" is included in the input prompt of the fzf-lua plugin for Neovim. It's unclear exactly when this started happening.\r\n\r\n![swappy-20250102-201624](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d60de3ac-46a8-49c5-8e4e-b32f260a13ef)\r\n\r\nThe issue does not occur when the mini.basics plugin is disabled.\r\n\r\nThank you.\n\n### Neovim version\n\nv0.10.2\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\ninstall mini.basics\r\ninstall fzf-lua\r\n\r\nRegister `files` as a shortcut to the leader key and open the window.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\n_No response_\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nThe input prompt should be clean and empty, but a floating window is created with the letter `i` already entered.",
